    "rationale": "October design (docs/adsb_nn/design_report_1.json): 20 design fits. Piecewise-linear embeddings beat scalar rank inputs (rank -0.07% committee blend); target clipping at 5400 s, lr 5e-4, 1024x4 with dropout 0.2, dropout 0.2 + weight decay 1e-3 and a 10-epoch budget all blend worse; clipping at 21600 s, weight EMA, clip+EMA, 16-dim numeric and 32-dim categorical embeddings are within the base seed noise (single base seeds -0.73..-1.00%). Seed averaging dominates: the mean of 2/4/8 base seeds blends at -1.12/-1.25/-1.44% (committee level, best weight 0.35/0.40/0.45) and -0.50/-0.57/-0.66% on the October recipe proxy (best weight 0.40/0.45/0.50, flat between 0.45 and 0.55). TabM-mini k=4 is the best single network (167.49) but blends at -0.89% with error correlation 0.925 at ~3.2x the compute of a base seed, below two base seeds (-1.12%) - so the declared network is the base recipe with 16 fresh seeds (101-116), and the declared shares are 0.3/0.4/0.5/0.6 around the recipe optimum. The second tabm4 design seed was still running at declaration time and is reported as an addendum; it cannot change this choice.",
